# A `WHILE`/`UNTIL` condition that calls or sends runs from the loop's test
# region; `TRACE I` walks it. Each stanza answers what the walked condition
# answered.

# a sending WHILE re-tested at the DO, after an END and after an ITERATE,
# under trace r: the `>K>` of each test follows the method's own clauses
program
trace r
o = .c~new
do while o~more
  if o~n = 2 then iterate
  say o~n
end
exit
::class c
::method init
  expose n
  n = 0
::method more
  expose n
  n = n + 1
  return n < 4
::method n
  expose n
  return n
